From: ProjectM TV maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve original left-axis legacy equation angle seam

Original MilkDrop2 plugin.cpp supplies atan2f(+0,negative)=+pi to
legacy per-pixel equations. Current physical mapping negates that cached
angle to -pi at the exact left axis, changing nonperiodic predicates.
Retain the cached angle only for exact legacy/default/fallback left-axis
nodes; preserve negation off axis and throughout the actual custom path.
Copy the signed cached angle rather than normalizing it: a frozen -0
axis cache pair retains original atan2f(-0,negative)=-pi consumption.

Keep raw radius/angle shader attributes, original coordinates, topology,
traversal, static cache/upload, CPU rotation trig/signed zoom power,
point/equation counts and one-producer prepared replay unchanged.
No epsilon, added atan2, extra evaluation, target, buffer or pass.
Finite qualification: generated even mesh, positive finite aspect factors.
Custom-warp VS oracle and nonfinite/unsupported aspect domains are excluded.

Original: vis_milk2/plugin.cpp:2272-2285 and milkdropfs.cpp:1839-1842;
byte-identical original2.25c and local milkdrop2/src sources.

diff --git a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/PerPixelMesh.cpp b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/PerPixelMesh.cpp
--- a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/PerPixelMesh.cpp
+++ b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/PerPixelMesh.cpp
@@ -281,7 +281,10 @@
                 *perPixelContext.x = static_cast<double>(curVertex.X() * 0.5f * presetState.renderContext.aspectX + 0.5f);
                 *perPixelContext.y = static_cast<double>(curVertex.Y() * 0.5f * presetState.renderContext.aspectY + 0.5f);
                 *perPixelContext.rad = static_cast<double>(curRadiusAngle.radius);
-                *perPixelContext.ang = static_cast<double>(-curRadiusAngle.angle);
+                // Preserve original atan2 signed-zero seam on the exact legacy left axis.
+                // Keep off-axis mapping and the custom shader/equation producer unchanged.
+                const bool legacyLeftAxis = !m_warpShader && curVertex.X() < 0.0f && curVertex.Y() == 0.0f;
+                *perPixelContext.ang = static_cast<double>(legacyLeftAxis ? curRadiusAngle.angle : -curRadiusAngle.angle);
                 *perPixelContext.zoom = static_cast<double>(*perFrameContext.zoom);
                 *perPixelContext.zoomexp = static_cast<double>(*perFrameContext.zoomexp);
                 *perPixelContext.rot = static_cast<double>(*perFrameContext.rot);
